-# (0240) Route a FrameHeap arena-grow overflow to the global ExpHeap.
+# (0240, corrected by 0241) Route a FrameHeap arena-grow overflow to the global ExpHeap.
 # Root cause (REPORT-0234-PROBE-DATA-ANALYSIS.md, device-probed by the 0234
 # probe in V1.3.62, three runs): the SARC-loading container is a
 # sead::FrameHeap, a fixed-length frame heap (+0xe0 head, +0xe8 tail). Its
@@ -562,44 +562,63 @@ def _headkey_fallback_frame_step(ctx):
 # site that does not fire for the SARC grow (count 4096 passes the tst
 # check at 0x954368) and is left alone.
 # The cut replaces the `blr x8` at 0x954484 with `b <trampoline>`. The
-# trampoline tries the global heap's allocate (vtable+0x30, the same
-# interface the dispatcher 0x93eb50 uses: `ldr x8,[x1]; ldr x3,[x8,#0x30];
-# br x3`, called as (allocator, size, count)) on the global heap x25, which
-# is the FrameHeap's backing store (an ExpHeap). On success it jumps to
-# 0x95448c, the unlock-if-locked branch (`cbnz x19,#0x95449c`), and the
-# epilogue returns the pointer in x23 -- NOT to 0x954488 (which zeroes x23)
-# and NOT to 0x9544a4 (which skips the unlock). On failure (ExpHeap returns
-# 0) it calls V directly from the trampoline, with the grow request rebuilt
-# (`ldr x0,[x25,#0x10]` for the heap interface, `add x1,sp,#8` for
-# &grow_request); V aborts, exactly as before. It does NOT branch back to
-# 0x954478: the cut at 0x954484 replaced the `blr x8`, so returning there
-# would re-enter the trampoline and loop forever on failure.
-# Register safety: at the cut x25 is the global heap, x22 the size, w20 the
-# count and x19 the lock flag (0, or &mutex at container+0x98), all
-# callee-saved and preserved across the trampoline's `blr` (which clobbers
-# only caller-saved registers and x30; the allocator's x30 is saved on its
-# stack and restored by the epilogue). The trampoline writes only x0/x1/x2/
-# x8 (caller-saved, dead after the V call in the original code) and x23
-# (the return value, set deliberately). sp is never touched, so the grow
-# request at [sp,#8] is intact for the fail path.
+# trampoline gets the current heap via sead::getCurrentHeap (0x9564a0) --
+# the same function the dispatcher 0x93eb50 calls when the allocator arg is
+# NULL -- then calls that heap's allocate (vtable+0x30, the same interface
+# the dispatcher uses: `ldr x8,[x1]; ldr x3,[x8,#0x30]; br x3`, called as
+# (allocator, size, count)). (0241 CORRECTS 0240 here: 0240 did
+# `ldr x8,[x25]` / `ldr x8,[x8,#0x30]`, treating [x25] as a vtable, but
+# [x25] is struct S's first field (offset 0) = DATA, not a vtable -- it read
+# S+0x30 as the allocate function and jumped to a .data address. Device
+# proof: DmIOS-2026-11-24-154754.ips, V1.3.63 Football run, EXC_BAD_ACCESS /
+# KERN_PROTECTION_FAILURE at 0x11019a0e8, CODESIGNING "Invalid Page",
+# backtrace frame 1 = 0x97e278, x0=x25=0x1104AE080, x8=PC=0x11019a0e8. The
+# 0240 concept (overflow -> ExpHeap) is right; only the lookup was wrong.)
+# Guard: if the current heap IS the FrameHeap (x21), the trampoline does
+# NOT use it (that would re-enter this allocator and the trampoline
+# forever); it falls back to V instead. On success it jumps to 0x95448c,
+# the unlock-if-locked branch (`cbnz x19,#0x95449c`), and the epilogue
+# returns the pointer in x23 -- NOT to 0x954488 (which zeroes x23) and NOT
+# to 0x9544a4 (which skips the unlock). On failure (current heap is NULL,
+# or is the FrameHeap, or allocate returns 0) it calls V directly from the
+# trampoline, with the grow request rebuilt (`ldr x0,[x25,#0x10]` for the
+# heap interface, `add x1,sp,#8` for &grow_request); V aborts, exactly as
+# before. It does NOT branch back to 0x954478: the cut at 0x954484 replaced
+# the `blr x8`, so returning there would re-enter the trampoline and loop
+# forever on failure.
+# Register safety: at the cut x25 is the struct S pointer, x22 the size,
+# w20 the count and x19 the lock flag (0, or &mutex at container+0x98), all
+# callee-saved and preserved across the trampoline's `bl`/`blr` calls
+# (0x9564a0 preserves x19 and the AAPCS64 callee-saved registers x19-x28;
+# the allocator's x30 is saved on its stack at [sp,#0x70] and restored by
+# the epilogue at 0x95448c, so the trampoline's `bl`/`blr` clobbering x30 is
+# harmless -- the trampoline JUMPS to 0x95448c, it does not `ret`). The
+# trampoline writes only x0/x1/x2/x8 (caller-saved, dead after the V call in
+# the original code) and x23 (the return value, set deliberately). sp is
+# never touched, so the grow request at [sp,#8] is intact for the fail path
+# (0x9564a0 uses its own stack frame and restores sp before returning).
+# UNPINNED: whether 0x9564a0 returns the ExpHeap (the desired case) or the
+# FrameHeap in the SARC-load context on FileLoadThread cannot be decided
+# from static disassembly alone (the SARC loader does not call
+# setCurrentHeap, so the current heap is the thread's ambient heap; the
+# guard covers the FrameHeap case by falling back to V, so the fix is safe
+# either way, but if the current heap IS the FrameHeap the costumes still
+# abort and the fix does not help). The mock verifies the logic on host
+# values only. Device acceptance: Explorer / Football / Mechanic enter a
+# kingdom without the abort backtrace and without a codesigning kill, and
+# the good costumes (Happi / Hakama / Armor / Painter) are unaffected (they
+# never reach the overflow path, so this cut is a no-op for them).
 # Cost (intentional, by design): the ExpHeap block is never freed by the
 # FrameHeap reset, so each overflowing SARC load leaks ~1 MB (925,888 /
 # 946,368 bytes); a few MB per game session at most. The SARC data is just
 # bytes, so loading it from the ExpHeap instead of the FrameHeap changes
 # nothing the loader reads.
-# The 0234 grow probe (0230 diagnostic) is REMOVED by this patch: its two
-# cuts (0x954478, 0x954390) and its body are deleted, and its mission is
-# complete (the probe data pinned the root cause). The B cut at 0x97e114
-# (0234 diagnostic) is KEPT: it writes to the same ring (state +0x3B20,
-# kept below for it) and does not conflict with this cut. The 0228 headkey
-# probe and the 0239 head-only fallback are untouched.
-# UNPINNED: the ExpHeap allocate at [x25] vtable+0x30 is inferred from the
-# dispatcher interface (0x93eb50, same `ldr x3,[x8,#0x30]` shape) and has
-# NOT been called on a real device; the mock verifies the logic on host
-# values only. Device acceptance: Explorer / Football / Mechanic enter a
-# kingdom without the abort backtrace, and the good costumes (Happi /
-# Hakama / Armor / Painter) are unaffected (they never reach the overflow
-# path, so this cut is a no-op for them).
+# The 0234 grow probe (0230 diagnostic) was REMOVED by 0240 and stays
+# removed: its two cuts (0x954478, 0x954390) and its body are deleted, and
+# its mission is complete (the probe data pinned the root cause). The B cut
+# at 0x97e114 (0234 diagnostic) is KEPT: it writes to the same ring (state
+# +0x3B20, kept below for it) and does not conflict with this cut. The 0228
+# headkey probe and the 0239 head-only fallback are untouched.
 # The ring constants below are kept for the B cut (0234 diagnostic), which
 # writes its records to the same ring at state +0x3B20.
 DIAG_GROW_RING_OFF = 0x3B20
@@ -616,16 +635,40 @@ def _arena_expheap_frame_step(ctx):
     def _w(word): body.append(('w', word))
     def _label(name): labels[name] = len(body)
     def _cbz(rt, label): body.append(('cbz', rt, label))
+    def _beq(label): body.append(('beq', label))
+    def _bl_abs(target): body.append(('bl_abs', target))
     def _b_abs(target): body.append(('b_abs', target))
-    # Try the global heap's allocate (vtable+0x30) for the overflowing
-    # request. x25 = global heap, x22 = size, x20 = count, x19 = lock flag.
-    _w(LDRX(8, 25, 0))          # x8 = [x25] (global heap vtable)
-    _w(LDRX(8, 8, 6))           # x8 = [x8, #0x30] (allocate)
-    _w(MOV(0, 25))              # x0 = allocator (global heap)
+    # (0241) Get the current heap via sead::getCurrentHeap (0x9564a0) -- the
+    # same function the dispatcher 0x93eb50 calls when the allocator arg is
+    # NULL -- then call that heap's allocate (vtable+0x30). x25 = struct S
+    # pointer (the arg 0x9564a0 takes, as the dispatcher passes it), x22 =
+    # size, x20 = count, x21 = FrameHeap container, x19 = lock flag.
+    # The 0240 trampoline is WRONG and is replaced here: it did
+    # `ldr x8,[x25]` / `ldr x8,[x8,#0x30]`, treating [x25] as a vtable, but
+    # [x25] is struct S's first field (offset 0) = DATA, not a vtable, so it
+    # read S+0x30 as the allocate function and jumped to a .data address.
+    # Device proof (DmIOS-2026-11-24-154754.ips, V1.3.63 Football run):
+    # EXC_BAD_ACCESS / KERN_PROTECTION_FAILURE at 0x11019a0e8, CODESIGNING
+    # "Invalid Page", faulting thread FileLoadThread, backtrace frame 1 =
+    # 0x97e278 (right after the SARC allocate call), x0=x25=0x1104AE080,
+    # x1=946368 (Football SARC size), x2=4096, x8=PC=0x11019a0e8. The 0240
+    # CONCEPT (overflow -> ExpHeap) is right; only the vtable lookup was
+    # wrong. The correct lookup is via 0x9564a0 (which the allocator itself
+    # never calls, but the dispatcher does -- see 0x93eb50).
+    # Guard: if the current heap IS the FrameHeap (x21), do NOT use it --
+    # that would re-enter this allocator (0x954310) and the trampoline
+    # forever. Fall back to V (abort, as before) instead.
+    _w(MOV(0, 25))              # x0 = struct S pointer (arg for 0x9564a0)
+    _bl_abs(0x9564a0)           # bl 0x9564a0 (x0 = current heap)
+    _cbz(0, 'fail')             # current heap is NULL -> fall back to V
+    _w(CMPR(0, 21))             # cmp x0, x21 (is the current heap the FrameHeap?)
+    _beq('fail')                # yes -> fall back to V (do NOT recurse)
     _w(MOV(1, 22))              # x1 = size
-    _w(MOV(2, 20))              # x2 = count
-    _w(BLR(8))                  # blr x8 (ExpHeap allocate; x0 = pointer or 0)
-    _cbz(0, 'fail')             # ExpHeap returned 0 -> fall back to V
+    _w(MOV(2, 20))              # x2 = count (x20's upper bits are zero -- set by `mov w20, w2` at 0x95435c -- so this is the zero-extended count, as the dispatcher's `mov w2, w19`)
+    _w(LDRX(8, 0, 0))           # x8 = [x0] (current heap vtable)
+    _w(LDRX(8, 8, 6))           # x8 = [x8, #0x30] (allocate)
+    _w(BLR(8))                  # blr x8 (allocate(heap, size, count); x0 = pointer or 0)
+    _cbz(0, 'fail')             # allocate returned 0 -> fall back to V
     _w(MOV(23, 0))              # x23 = pointer (the allocator's return value)
     _b_abs(0x95448c)            # unlock-if-locked branch, then epilogue returns x23
     _label('fail')
